<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyen Hoang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1525">1525</a>–<a href="/years/1613">1613</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyen Hoang was the first of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyen lords</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. In 1558, to escape his rivals the Trinh lords, he had himself appointed governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuan-hoa">Thuan Hoa</a> in central Vietnam. He built up an autonomous southern realm, Dang Trong, that expanded at the expense of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, and his descendants later founded the Nguyen dynasty, Vietnam's last imperial house.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nguyen-hoang.jpg" alt="Nguyen Hoang" width="202" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nguyễn Hoàng Quý · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nguyen_hoang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
